Create /etc/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy.cfg, see oauth2-proxy.cfg.example in
/usr/share/doc/oauth2-proxy-* and https://oauth2-proxy.github.io/oauth2-proxy/

For more instances, use /etc/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy.<name>.cfg with:
- OpenRC: ln -s oauth2-proxy /etc/init.d/oauth2-proxy.<name>
- systemd: systemctl enable --now oauth2-proxy@<name>.service

OpenRC runs the service as nobody:nobody, so keep the config root:nobody 0640.
systemd runs it with DynamicUser and passes the config as a credential, so the
config can stay root:root 0600.
